# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CMake build trees
#
# Every preset in CMakePresets.json puts its build tree at build/<presetName>,
# so `build/` alone covers dev, vs, ci-linux, ci-macos, ci-windows, strict,
# strict-ci and spikes. `out/` is what Visual Studio's "Open Folder" mode uses
# instead when it ignores the preset binaryDir, and cmake-build*/ is CLion's.
build/
out/
cmake-build*/

# In-source-configure droppings. The root CMakeLists refuses an in-source build,
# but a `cmake .` typed before that guard existed still leaves these behind, and
# nobody should have to notice them in `git status` while cleaning up.
#
# Note there is deliberately NO bare `Makefile` rule here (WFS-DIY carries one):
# it would silently hide a hand-written top-level Makefile, and this repo has no
# generated one to hide — the presets all use Ninja or Visual Studio.
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
cmake_install.cmake

# CMakeUserPresets.json is the per-developer companion to the TRACKED
# CMakePresets.json: the file where you put your own generator, your local
# toolchain path, your -D overrides. It must never be committed — a committed
# one overrides everyone else's environment with yours.
CMakeUserPresets.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Compile-database / indexer output
#
# CMAKE_EXPORT_COMPILE_COMMANDS=ON is set in the `base` preset, so every build
# tree has a compile_commands.json; the top-level one is the symlink or copy
# people make for clangd.
compile_commands.json
.cache/

# ccache, when CCACHE_DIR is pointed at the workspace (as CI does)
.ccache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# IDE and editor
.vs/
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Agent working files, untracked by policy. Note this ignores the `.claude/`
# DIRECTORY only — a top-level CLAUDE.md is a tracked project document (the
# devplan makes it PRD 4 verbatim) and must be able to land.
.claude/
tmpclaude-*
**/tmpclaude-*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python (scripts/check-pins.py and whatever joins it)
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS cruft
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
ehthumbs.db
Thumbs.db

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Forward-looking: the Phase 7 tablet client (PRD 3.17) gets its own toolchain
# under clients/tablet/ and is never an add_subdirectory of this build. These two
# rules exist NOW so that the first `npm install` run in that tree cannot be
# committed by accident — a node_modules/ in the history is permanent.
node_modules/
dist/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT ignored, on purpose — if you are about to add one of these, don't:
#   docs/**    the PRD and the devplan are the spec and are tracked
#   *.md       ditto, plus README / THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES / the spike reports
#   /CLAUDE*   see above
#   ThirdParty/  the submodule gitlinks are tracked; the working trees are not
#                files git sees, so no rule is needed for them either way
